 ### Other features
 
+- `jpeg_2000_rust` selects the experimental `jpeg2000-decoder` backend
+  for JPEG 2000 decoding instead of `hayro-jpeg2000`. It is not enabled by
+  default and requires Rust 1.88 or later. It supports grayscale and RGB
+  output, including straight alpha, and preserves explicitly declared,
+  full-resolution unsigned 8-bit CMYK. When strict mode is disabled, Part 1
+  inputs use bounded recovery and clean JPX inputs use the normal JPX-capable
+  decoder. The backend does not apply ICC profiles. In lenient mode only, it
+  warns and interprets plain three- or four-channel 8-bit JP2 samples as RGB or
+  CMYK when the color box uses method 3 or its method-2 ICC header is truncated.
+  The lossless test fixtures come from the
+  [`jpeg2000_rs` synthetic image tests](https://github.com/microsoft/jpeg2000_rs/tree/01f7687/adapters/image/tests/fixtures).
+
 - `serde`: Enable serde support for serializing image metadata, adds `serde` as a dependency
 - `log`: Enable printing information via `log` crate
 - `simd`: Enable SIMD support for certain image operations,
